    {
      "is": "IS 4895:1985",
      "clause": "4",
      "title": "Grades",
      "text": "4. Grades— The logs of 2.5 m length shall be graded as below depending on cumulative value of the permissible defects: Grade 1 — No single log shall contain more than 2.5 units of defects. Grade 2 — No single log shall contain more than 5 units of defects Grade 3 — No single log shall contain more than 7.5 units of defects For  logs more than 2.5 m in length, the limits given above shall be derived by the following equation; Permissible number of defects in logs more than  2.5 m in length = Where L — length of  log in m, and P — permissible defect value for 2.5 m in length.",
      "clause_id": "IS 4895:1985#4",
      "family": "IS 4895",
      "year": 1985,
